# CASM Phase 12 WP69 trusted reference: casmchar1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmchar1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves a
# character literal produces correct bytes when reached through the real
# production parser/emitter (posImmediateChar in parser.s, emitByteList's
# own short-circuit in emit.s) -- both call sites bypass exprEvaluate
# entirely (this WP's own scoping decision), so this is the only live
# proof of that wiring; expr.s itself is unchanged.
#
# Source (.ORG $C000, fixed address -- no relocatable symbols involved):
#   LDA #'A'         ; immediate, character literal = $41
#   .BYTE 'H', 'I'   ; directive operands, character literals = $48, $49
#
# Source 'A'/'H'/'I' are plain ASCII uppercase in the fixture text, which
# is numerically identical to unshifted PETSCII ($41-$5A) -- no charmap
# translation applies to a raw .seq fixture (unlike a ca65-assembled .s
# harness), and a character literal's content byte is taken verbatim, no
# case folding either way.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 C0     PRG load-address header ($C000, little-endian)
#   A9 41     LDA #$41   ('A')
#   48 49     .BYTE $48, $49   ('H', 'I')
#
# bytes: 6
# sha256: d577678cfdb724abb98567175953319106cb2577c3ba1158334b52faad87935a
# source_sha256: casmchar1.seq=fc8784bbaf7b3b205b2cebaf303a84952b1e2bb0c47576b8e7b99c5ea540ef13
# Independent byte derivation reviewed and approved by the user 2026-09-02
